      // drops and in `consumed_var_pending_drops` — e.g. `return(out)` for an
      // OWNED local inside a branch: `out` is dup'd for the caller (rc 1->2),
      // the early-return drop releases the local (2->1, correct), and then the
      // consumed-var escape drop released it AGAIN (1->0), so the function
      // returned a FREED pointer. Exclude anything already dropped just above —
      // a second release of the same variable in one return sequence can only
      // ever be a double free. Mirrors the same fix in return.ts; see
      // issues/fixed/yo-return-owned-local-in-branch-double-drop.md (this is
      // what made tests/fs/dir.test.yo HANG: state_code_gen.yo's
